          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Frozen Seafood Can Be Fresher Than &ldquo;Fresh&rdquo;",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "t_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>For decades, the seafood counter has carried an unspoken assumption: frozen means compromised, while &ldquo;fresh&rdquo; represents seafood at its best.</p><p>But &ldquo;never frozen&rdquo; does not necessarily mean recently harvested. Fresh seafood may spend days moving through processors, distributors, airplanes, trucks, and display cases &mdash; all while flavor and texture race against the clock.</p><p>Seatopia takes a different approach. We work with transparent, traceable aquaculture farms that freeze seafood as close to harvest as possible. Rapid freezing slows the processes that diminish quality, preserving the character of the fish until you are ready to enjoy it.</p><p><strong>Think of it as culinary time travel: peak freshness, paused.</strong></p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
