    "footprint": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "h_footprint": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "A More Mindful Journey",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "t_footprint": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Highly perishable &ldquo;fresh&rdquo; seafood often depends on speed, frequent deliveries, and &mdash; in some international supply chains &mdash; carbon-intensive air freight. Frozen seafood can travel through slower, more efficient logistics while maintaining quality.</p><p>A European seafood supply-chain assessment estimated that air-freighted seafood can exceed 10 kilograms of CO2-equivalent per kilogram of product on some routes. The same assessment found refrigerated sea transport may produce only a small fraction of the emissions associated with air cargo, although the impact of any product depends on its complete supply chain.</p><p>A longer usable life can also help reduce avoidable waste. You thaw only the portions you intend to prepare, while the rest remains protected in the freezer.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
